{"diagnosis": "Loopback TX stayed idle so ser_tx=1 and RX got 0xff vs want 0xa5 at TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xff want 0xa5. With divider 64 from picosoc/picosoc.v:120 and picosoc/picosoc.v:197 reg_div_we path, TX bit timer at picosoc/simpleuart.v:130 uses (cfg_divider >> 4) making TX ~16x too fast, so the RX sampler misses the start/data bits and reads idle. Fix is to use full cfg_divider for the TX bit period.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -125,10 +125,10 @@
 			if (reg_dat_we && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, reg_dat_di[7:0], 1'b0};
 				send_bitcnt <= 10;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end else
-			if (send_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) && send_bitcnt) begin
+			if (send_divcnt > cfg_divider && send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= {1'b1, send_pattern[9:1]};
 				send_bitcnt <= send_bitcnt - 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 			end", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP, uart loopback 0xa5 received correctly"}

